WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:22.680
Some miniature cast 12 M proteins can cut DNA after all, clarifying structural features that enable activity. This is Planetterrian Daily, Episode 256. After that, protein organ clocks for disease forecasts, DNA cubes that lock into three-dimensional shapes, and edible fungus grown from carbon dioxide, then spotlight and a closer look at insects on the wing.

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:29.660
Hayato Morinaga, Satoshi Enomora, and Osamu Nureki led an international team at the University

00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:35.500
of Tokyo that mapped atomic scale differences between active and inactive CAS-12M forms

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:41.360
with cryo-electron microscopy in a Nature Chemical Biology paper covered by Fizz.org.

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:46.980
They found amino acid substitutions that restore cleavage in UN CAS-12M4A.

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:51.500
Those substitutions give design rules for compact genome editing tools.

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:57.591
Protein organ clocks, both measured and inferred, raised five-year prediction accuracy for

00:00:57.591 --> 00:01:02.071
multiple diseases when they were added to electronic health records, in work published

00:01:02.071 --> 00:01:03.751
in science translational medicine.

00:01:04.371 --> 00:01:06.531
The gain showed up in two large cohorts.

00:01:07.091 --> 00:01:09.291
Records on their own did not capture that signal.

00:01:09.991 --> 00:01:14.891
Rabbit technology infers protein levels from routine data, and that inferred signal is

00:01:14.891 --> 00:01:16.591
what the clocks pull into the forecast.

00:01:16.591 --> 00:01:23.661
Associate Professor Pettersolk's team, in a report carried by Fizz.org, built a programmable

00:01:23.661 --> 00:01:27.461
set of DNA cubes that assemble into complex three-dimensional shapes.

00:01:28.061 --> 00:01:31.781
The cubes lock together on principles similar to Minecraft block placement.

00:01:32.321 --> 00:01:37.721
The method opens routes to nanorobots, layered electronics, and other advanced nanoscale devices.

00:01:38.381 --> 00:01:43.381
Waste carbon dioxide, light and microbes produce a protein-rich edible fungus within

00:01:43.381 --> 00:01:44.081
seven days.

00:01:44.081 --> 00:01:48.421
The setup bypasses the land and water that conventional crops demand.

00:01:49.001 --> 00:01:53.781
It is aimed at projected shortfalls in agricultural protein output by 2050.

00:01:54.561 --> 00:01:59.361
Patients who underwent robot-assisted knee replacement reported equivalent pain, mobility

00:01:59.361 --> 00:02:04.241
and recovery at one year to patients treated with conventional surgery in a large clinical

00:02:04.241 --> 00:02:05.981
trial covered by science daily.

00:02:06.541 --> 00:02:08.461
The robots improve surgical precision.

00:02:09.041 --> 00:02:13.021
Those precision gains produce no measurable clinical difference after 12 months.

00:02:13.021 --> 00:02:13.201
citizens.

00:02:13.341 --> 00:02:18.101
City storages, University of London, tested whether dislike of artificial intelligence

00:02:18.101 --> 00:02:23.301
or AI reduces its effect on choices, in work carried by Fizz.org.

00:02:24.181 --> 00:02:28.461
Participants who expressed aversion still altered decisions when AI input was provided.

00:02:28.981 --> 00:02:32.521
Negative attitudes did not block the technology's sway over behavior.

00:02:33.201 --> 00:02:38.101
Brown fat activity stayed unchanged even as a tested compound increased whole-body energy

00:02:38.101 --> 00:02:40.401
expenditure, according to Science Daily.

00:02:40.401 --> 00:02:45.001
The result points to an additional still unidentified route for calorie burning.

00:02:45.421 --> 00:02:49.341
The finding complicates efforts to harness brown fat for obesity treatment.

00:02:49.861 --> 00:02:55.021
Certain fungi trigger formation of new water-carrying cells and plants, according to an international

00:02:55.021 --> 00:02:59.681
team led by the University of Gottingen, in work carried by Fizz.org.

00:03:00.321 --> 00:03:03.341
Infected plants displayed greater tolerance to drought stress.

00:03:03.901 --> 00:03:09.281
A single fungal protein drives the mechanism, and the report appears in cell host and microbe.

00:03:09.281 --> 00:03:14.421
Carbon nanotube electrons followed a quantum model rather than a classical one in measurements

00:03:14.421 --> 00:03:17.721
by a group from Lithuania, Finland, and Israel.

00:03:18.381 --> 00:03:22.381
Experiments and theory together showed that the quantum description governs collective

00:03:22.381 --> 00:03:23.321
electron motion.

00:03:23.961 --> 00:03:28.301
The work is the first direct demonstration of which physical framework governs that motion.

00:03:29.061 --> 00:03:34.261
Imperial College London researchers identified a compound that restores Cyprophloxus in activity

00:03:34.261 --> 00:03:38.721
against methicillin-resistant Staphylococcus aureus, or MRSA.

00:03:39.381 --> 00:03:43.981
The inhibitor targets a resistance mechanism and resensitizes the bacteria in laboratory

00:03:43.981 --> 00:03:44.581
tests.

00:03:45.101 --> 00:03:49.021
The finding offers a route to extend the useful life of existing antibiotics.

00:03:49.901 --> 00:03:54.981
Paragreen falcons stand to gain a 74% rise in suitable United Kingdom territory by

00:03:54.981 --> 00:03:58.361
2018 in modeling of a high-emission scenario.

00:03:59.041 --> 00:04:02.261
Shifting temperature and precipitation patterns drive that expansion.

00:04:02.261 --> 00:04:07.761
White-tailed eagles and other raptors face substantial range contraction under the same projections.

00:04:08.703 --> 00:04:15.023
Partners who find each other's natural body odor pleasant report higher levels of sexual intimacy and satisfaction.

00:04:15.723 --> 00:04:21.823
Otter compatibility sits in the sensory basis for long-term pair bonding rather than as a signal to be masked.

00:04:22.403 --> 00:04:28.823
Participants rated odor pleasantness separately from visual or personality traits, which isolated its contribution.

00:04:28.823 --> 00:04:33.603
The work points to a role for olfaction in human relationship maintenance that has been

00:04:33.603 --> 00:04:34.443
easy to miss.

00:04:35.023 --> 00:04:39.923
Researchers at the University of Exeter sampled two dragonfly species at a Pyrenees mountain

00:04:39.923 --> 00:04:42.743
pass, with the study published in Ecography.

00:04:43.363 --> 00:04:48.023
Nine in ten lesser emperors and seven in ten daughters had taken known migrants as prey.

00:04:48.583 --> 00:04:52.083
A subset of the lesser emperors had eaten smaller, darker dragonflies.

00:04:52.663 --> 00:04:56.063
The sampling records a food web in the air among animals on migration.

00:04:56.063 --> 00:05:01.805
Most people assume migrating animals travel in neat parallel columns and barely interact

00:05:01.805 --> 00:05:03.245
with other species on the way.

00:05:03.985 --> 00:05:06.005
Meals recovered from the guts show the reverse.

00:05:06.705 --> 00:05:11.605
Migrants concentrate in space and in time, and that crowding builds layered predator-pray

00:05:11.605 --> 00:05:12.785
relationships in flight.

00:05:13.705 --> 00:05:17.765
Insects that cross garden and farmland and autumn are feeding while other migrants feed

00:05:17.765 --> 00:05:18.185
on them.

00:05:18.805 --> 00:05:23.305
Genetic barcoding of DNA from the guts turned up 87 distinct prey animals.

00:05:23.305 --> 00:05:27.805
Flies were the largest share of every meal and turned up in every gut they read.

00:05:28.145 --> 00:05:32.645
That tally is what a single narrow pass can produce when it funnels enough biomass to

00:05:32.645 --> 00:05:35.765
support a feeding web rather than isolated travelers.

00:05:36.325 --> 00:05:41.265
Protecting migratory corridors also safeguards the hidden trophic links that move with the insects.

00:05:42.005 --> 00:05:46.345
Losing those corridors would remove both the prey base and the predators that rely on

00:05:46.345 --> 00:05:47.585
it during seasonal passage.

00:05:47.585 --> 00:05:54.818
In brief, myocardial infarction with non-obstructive coronary arteries, or Minoka, is the subject

00:05:54.818 --> 00:05:59.958
of a Lancet review that summarizes current understanding and flags gaps in treatment evidence.

00:06:00.798 --> 00:06:06.198
Cardiometabolic drivers of heart failure with preserved ejection fraction, or HFP-EF,

00:06:06.598 --> 00:06:10.758
are examined in a comprehensive nature review that also sets out the limits of current

00:06:10.758 --> 00:06:11.598
classification.

00:06:11.598 --> 00:06:18.898
A 30-year study of more than 1,500 adults aged 65 and older, reported by lifespan.io,

00:06:19.438 --> 00:06:23.878
linked persistent loneliness but not occasional episodes to higher dementia incidents.

00:06:24.378 --> 00:06:28.678
Testing described by the Harvard Gazette revealed undisclosed pharmaceutical compounds

00:06:28.678 --> 00:06:33.658
in some unregulated over-the-counter skin treatments that carry potential medical risks.

00:06:34.198 --> 00:06:39.398
Gene therapy was placed in a direct comparison carried by uric alert against mitochondrial

00:06:39.398 --> 00:06:44.078
transplantation for correcting age-related mitochondrial dysfunction in model systems.

00:06:44.718 --> 00:06:50.558
Excess intake of a common nutrient in observational data covered by science daily was associated

00:06:50.558 --> 00:06:52.678
with accelerated stiffening of blood vessels.

00:06:53.238 --> 00:06:59.498
Before we go, the amino acid substitutions that restore cleavage in UNCAST 12M4A are now

00:06:59.498 --> 00:07:02.758
published as design rules for the next round of compact editors.

